{"title":"2026 USAMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Day_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Day_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 2</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_1\">Day 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Day 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be an integer greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. For which real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/c/d1c5ce64959e8d0ec178ac668ec7f8a42130fb97.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\lfloor nx\\rfloor-\\sum_{k=1}^n\\frac{\\lfloor kx\\rfloor}{k}\\]\" width=\"124\" height=\"48\" />\nmaximal, and what is the maximal value that this expression can take?\nNote: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f3a5f1bb872894c1dfdef6cc4c0be00307ddf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor z\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"27\" height=\"20\" /> denotes the greatest integer less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2026 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Annie is playing a game where she starts with a row of positive integers, written on a blackboard, each of which is a power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. On each turn, she can erase two adjacent numbers and replace them with a power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> that is greater than either of the erased numbers. This shortens the row of numbers, and she continues to take turns until only one number remains. Annie wins the game if the final remaining number is less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times the sum of the original numbers. Is it always possible for Annie to win, regardless of the starting row of numbers?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2026 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> be an acute scalene triangle with no angle equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/f/29fa0a9949f018e121b2093216dd5db13d3abef0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> be the circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/e/30e6bc175e2a4591ad2167ca267da27cb065adca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle_B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"29\" height=\"18\" /> be the equilateral triangle with three vertices on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />, one of which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/f/0ffb8fae480f25fbfb60dd7b827ea225e81b7f02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell_B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" /> be the line through the two vertices of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/e/30e6bc175e2a4591ad2167ca267da27cb065adca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle_B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"29\" height=\"18\" /> other than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/f/f2fd23bec5a71f3bc7898f703bd261ea0d1ea96f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle_C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"29\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/5/3856ff459e8e0f763e995fae8680728ba30beef3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell_C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" /> be defined analogously. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/f/0ffb8fae480f25fbfb60dd7b827ea225e81b7f02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell_B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" />, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> be the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/5/3856ff459e8e0f763e995fae8680728ba30beef3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell_C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoint of minor arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/b/f2b686e282112ee7338ebaf3427727ac8141c10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"15\" height=\"13\" /> be the triangle formed by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/f/0ffb8fae480f25fbfb60dd7b827ea225e81b7f02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell_B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/5/3856ff459e8e0f763e995fae8680728ba30beef3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell_C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" />, and the tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. Prove that the circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/0/620bb149eedce7c8570c99aafa2a8834e51fcc17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AYZ$\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" /> and the incircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/b/f2b686e282112ee7338ebaf3427727ac8141c10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"15\" height=\"13\" /> are tangent.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2026 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_2\">Day 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Day 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>A positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is called solitary if, for any nonnegative integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/4/6e42302f9dd0afe4a7cd50ac2115f72bee849423.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b=n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" />, either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> contains the digit <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> when written in base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Determine, with proof, the number of solitary integers less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/2/042b44ed762ce8a071b63c5b94d3adccd573ded3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^{2026}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2026 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> be a triangle. Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lie on sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/5/e657259c0995d2c36d46744bb4aa81471e6575ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, respectively, such that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/7/9f79a0be62330f80052b8447229914474e5e6903.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle AFE=\\angle BDF=\\angle CED.\\]\" width=\"221\" height=\"13\" />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/8/4d8aa423de2031c09aa06a1687767414dbb8120d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/0/0e0af44578003bbd64382d00ed07ed2e33099284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/2/be2b7d9af12c551508264ff8ed054503c4e1b890.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" /> be the circumcenters of triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/8/378fc67ebfe29ddad36d7bab7b5851c10738c166.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AFE$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/b/93b93a2dc17d4cf5e91cf1edaa02b2a16f690e42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BDF$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/5/dc5309b25510f426ca00c957623bd0396c79e4c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CED$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" />, respectively. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the circumcenters of triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/9/2e9e8b2c23e0545ef6de81f0ea578173e9ab7a64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DEF$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/5/b05c844d6d1a5d916d2a6a78d3a38ea13c28d1b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_AO_BO_C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"17\" />, respectively. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/c/00c790407cf1ea6e6b8dda1272b335c932ae1dea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OM=ON$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"91\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2026 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> be positive integers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/2/bd2e9fb001e4bae91c4a1af297fc7af1bcd469f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\varphi(ab+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"20\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/7/157b1248bad25e9621cdf712aa24411ec4698a84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2+b^2+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"85\" height=\"16\" />. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are Fibonacci numbers.\n</p><p>Note: Euler’s totient function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/d/63d7e990c9ebf7adc93ddd233b1239e5e4c0eef3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\varphi(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> is the number of positive integers less than\nor equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> that are relatively prime to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2026 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO\" title=\"2026 USAMO\">2026 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://ww